## Run in development

NatUI 0.2.x requires Node.js 22 or newer and a native host built from the
[NatUI framework repository](https://github.com/floklein/natui). Follow the
platform setup at [natui.dev](https://natui.dev), then set `NATUI_HOST` to the
built host executable when running this standalone project.

```bash
__INSTALL_COMMAND__
__RUN_COMMAND__ dev
```

The development server watches `src/main.tsx` and applies React Fast Refresh
to the existing native window.

## Application configuration

`natui.app.json` contains the application identity, source entry, output
directory, and platform icon paths. The generated icon files use native
container formats:

- `assets/AppIcon.icns` for macOS
- `assets/AppIcon.ico` with multiple resolutions for Windows

Replace both files with your final application artwork before distribution.
Keep the configured file formats, use complete PNG or JPEG 2000
representations inside the macOS `.icns`, and
include the platform-recommended sizes.

NatUI 0.2.x does not include native host source in `@natui/core`, so standalone
projects cannot package a native artifact yet. The configuration is ready for
the packager in a NatUI framework repository checkout.
